/E (Leather is primarily used in the production of footwear, accessories, and outerwear, representing a smaller segment of the overall textile market. Analyzing the leather supply chain reveals that the tanning process is the most polluting. Tanning involves treating animal hides with chemicals to make them resistant to water, heat, and abrasion. However, this process requires large amounts of water and results in high carbon emissions due to heavy chemical usage.)
